<urn:usf:contract:cli-diagnostic-classification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Classify a thrown error by whether it carries a stable machine-readable reason code, so a known semantic refusal reaches the operator as its actual reason and only a genuinely unexpected failure becomes INTERNAL_ERROR." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-diagnostic-classification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Observed while deriving Hermes work: a manifest declaring one graph IRI twice raised GraphLoadError carrying MANIFEST_DUPLICATE_SOURCE_OR_GRAPH, and the operator received \"Unexpected internal error\" with no reason code. Twenty domain error classes in src/ carry a reasonCode and none of them survive the boundary; only UsfError does." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-diagnostic-classification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "Local, hermetic and deterministic. It contacts no provider, reads no credential, mutates no historical source and writes only the declared paths." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
