<urn:usf:contract:cli-diagnostic-classification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Classification is not error handling. A refusal that reaches the boundary is still a refusal; this decides only how it is named, and a code it does not recognise stays INTERNAL_ERROR rather than being invented." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-diagnostic-classification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "No stack trace, file path, module name or internal message shape may become a reason code. The code must already exist as declared vocabulary on the error itself." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "cli-diagnostic-classification" <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "An error crossing the command boundary is a semantic refusal if and only if it carries a stable machine-readable reason code. A refusal is reported under that exact code; anything else is reported as INTERNAL_ERROR. The classifier must not derive a code from a message, a class name, a stack or any other implementation detail." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "known semantic refusal to its own stable reasonCode; unexpected implementation failure to INTERNAL_ERROR; never the reverse." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:verificationClass> <urn:usf:verification-class:dependency-declaration-integrity> <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:requirement:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Hermes cannot supervise autonomous realisation while semantic refusals are indistinguishable from crashes. A supervisor that cannot tell a refused manifest from a bug will retry the wrong thing." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:cli-diagnostic-classification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A UsfError reaches the boundary under its own code and exit code. A non-UsfError domain error carrying a reasonCode reaches the boundary under that reasonCode. A genuinely unexpected exception reaches the boundary as INTERNAL_ERROR with no internal detail. An error carrying a reasonCode that is not stable machine-readable vocabulary is treated as unexpected rather than surfaced. No message, stack, path or class name appears as a reason code in any case." <urn:usf:graph:cli-diagnostics> .
